   Entity, or having the power to direct its management and policies,
   whether through ownership, contract, or otherwise. Where the
   Licensee is an individual using the Software for Non-Commercial Use,
   the Organization is that individual.
   1.8. "Long-Term Contractor" means an individual who is not an
   employee but works for a member of the Organization on a full-time
   or substantially full-time basis (on average thirty (30) hours a
   week or more), whether engaged directly or through an agency, a
   personal company, or another intermediary, for a continuous period
   that has lasted, or is expected to last, six (6) months or more.
   1.9. "Employees" means the employees of every member of the
   Organization together with its Long-Term Contractors. The number of
   Employees is the number of employees stated in the most recent
   annual report or approved annual financial statements of the
   Organization (the consolidated figure where one is published,
   otherwise the sum of the figures for each member), plus the current
   number of Long-Term Contractors. For a member that has not yet
   published such a figure, a good-faith estimate of its current number
   of employees is used. The number of users, the volume of data, the
   number of Instances or Environments, and computing resources are not
   part of the number of Employees.
   1.10. "Micro-Company" means an Organization that meets both of the
   following conditions, which follow the definition of a
   microenterprise in Article 2(3) of the Annex to Commission
   Recommendation 2003/361/EC of 6 May 2003 concerning the definition
   of micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (OJ L 124, 20.5.2003,
   p. 36):
   (a) it has fewer than ten (10) Employees; and
   (b) its annual turnover or its annual balance sheet total does not
   exceed two million euros (EUR 2,000,000); it is enough that one of
   the two does not exceed that amount.
   The financial figures are those of the most recent approved
   accounting period of the whole Organization (consolidated where
   consolidated accounts are published, otherwise added up for each
   member), converted to euros where needed at the exchange rate of the
   last day of that period. For this License, the number of Employees
   under Section 1.9 is used as the staff headcount, so Long-Term
   Contractors count, and the Organization under Section 1.7 is used as
   the enterprise together with its linked enterprises. A public
   authority, a body governed by public law, and an Organization of
   which twenty-five percent (25%) or more of the capital or voting
   rights is controlled, directly or indirectly, jointly or
   individually, by one or more public bodies, are not Micro-Companies.
   An Organization with fewer than ten (10) Employees whose annual
   turnover and annual balance sheet total both exceed EUR 2,000,000 is
   not a Micro-Company (Section 4.4).
   1.11. "Educational Institution" means a school, college, or
   university that is accredited or officially recognized by the
   competent authority of its country to provide education or to award
   qualifications.
   1.12. "Non-Profit Organization" means a Legal Entity that is
   registered as a non-profit, charitable, or public-benefit
   organization under the law of the country where it is registered,
   and that does not distribute profits to its members, owners, or
   officers. It does not include public authorities or bodies governed
   by public law, other than Educational Institutions.
   1.13. "Non-Commercial Use" means use by an individual that is not
