2. Products

   2.1. Free Products
   The Free Products are:
   (a) SuperTable, the Python library published as the "supertable"
   package;
   (b) Data Island Core; and
   (c) Gatekeeper, the Data Island identity service.
   Free Products are free of charge for everyone (Section 4.1).

   2.2. Licensed Products
   The Licensed Products are:
   (a) Data Island Studio; and
   (b) Data Island Lighthouse.
   Licensed Products are free of charge in the cases set out in Section
   4.2 and require a Subscription otherwise (Section 4.3).

   2.3. Products Delivered Together
   A Free Product that is included in or delivered with a Licensed
   Product, such as the Data Island Core runtime inside Data Island
   Studio, remains a Free Product. Functionality of a Free Product that
   exists only to serve a Licensed Product, such as the Lighthouse tools
   that Data Island Core serves, may be used only by an Organization
   that is entitled to use that Licensed Product.

   2.4. Releases
   The list of Products in the version of this License that accompanies
   a release of a Product applies to that release (Section 10).

3. License Grant (Use Only)

   3.1. Grant
   Subject to Your compliance with this License, the Licensor grants
   You a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable
   license, for the duration set out in Section 3.5, to:
   (a) obtain the Software from the Licensor or from its official
   distribution channels;
   (b) install, deploy, and run unmodified copies of the Software
   inside Your Organization, and make the copies needed to do so,
   including backup and disaster-recovery copies;
   (c) build the Software from the unmodified source code that the
   Licensor provides (Section 6.2), and package unmodified Software
   together with other software, for example in a container image, for
   deployment inside Your Organization;
   (d) within the purpose and conditions of the grant in Section 4 that
   applies to You, use the Software for the internal purposes of Your
   Organization, including Production Use where Section 4 allows it,
   and to deliver Your own products and services, provided that they
   are not a Hosted Service or a Competing Product and that no Third
   Party receives a copy of the Software; and
   (e) copy the documentation, and adapt it for internal use, such as
   in runbooks and training materials for Your Authorized Users.

   3.2. Unlimited Scope
   Within the purpose and conditions of the grant in Section 4 that
   applies to You, You may run the Software on any number of Instances
   and Environments, for any number of Authorized Users, and with any
   volume of data, on infrastructure that Your Organization controls,
   or that is operated for it by the Licensor, by a partner under a
   Partner Agreement, or by a Service Provider under Section 5.5. No
   grant under this License is limited or priced by the number of
   users, the volume of data, the number of Instances or Environments,
   or the processors, memory, or other computing resources on which the
   Software runs.

   3.3. Your Own Programs
   You may write programs, scripts, notebooks, and queries that use the
   Software through its documented interfaces (such as its Python API,
   SQL, REST, OData, MCP, and command-line interfaces), declare the
   Software as a dependency of them, and copy the code examples in the
   documentation into them. Such programs are Your Content, provided
   that they do not contain a Modification of the Software.

   3.4. Use Only
   This License grants rights to use the Software as described in this
   Section 3. It does not grant any right to modify the Software, to
   create Derivative Works, or to distribute, sell, sublicense, or host
   the Software for Third Parties, except as this License or a Partner
   Agreement expressly allows.

   3.5. Duration
   The grant for the Free Products, and the grants of Section 4.2 for
   as long as their conditions are met, are perpetual unless terminated
   under Section 14. The grant under a Subscription lasts for the term
   of that Subscription.

4. Free and Paid Use

   4.1. Free Products (FREE FOR EVERYONE)
   Every individual and Legal Entity, of any size, may use the Free
   Products under Section 3 at no cost, for any purpose that Section 3
   allows, including Production Use.

   4.2. Licensed Products: Free Use (FREE)
   The following may use the Licensed Products under Section 3 at no
   cost:
   (a) Micro-Companies. A Micro-Company may use the Licensed Products
   for any business purpose that Section 3 allows, including Production
   Use, for as long as it remains a Micro-Company. If the Organization
   ceases to be a Micro-Company, it must, within thirty (30) days,
   obtain a Subscription, qualify under another grant in this Section
   4.2, or stop using the Licensed Products.
   (b) Evaluation. Any Organization, of any size, may use the Licensed
   Products for Evaluation for up to ninety (90) days from the earlier
   of the first installation of a Licensed Product by the Organization
   and the date on which the Licensor issues it an evaluation License
   Key. An Evaluation may use sample data, synthetic data, or copies of
   real data in non-production Environments. Each Organization has one
   Evaluation period, which covers the Licensed Products together.
   Extended or additional Evaluation periods require written
   authorization from the Licensor. When the Evaluation period ends,
   the Organization must obtain a Subscription, qualify under another
   grant in this Section 4.2, or stop using the Licensed Products.
   (c) Education. Educational Institutions, their enrolled students, and
   their educators may use the Licensed Products for:
       (i) classroom instruction and coursework;
       (ii) academic research and publications;
       (iii) student projects and thesis work;
       (iv) educational workshops and training; and
       (v) the Educational Institution's own internal administration.
   This grant does not cover commercial training programs offered for
   profit, or consulting, analytics, or IT services provided to Third
   Parties for a fee.
   (d) Non-Profit Organizations. A Non-Profit Organization may use the
   Licensed Products for its non-profit purposes and internal
   operations, including Production Use. This grant does not extend to
   its for-profit Affiliates, or to consulting, analytics, or IT
   services provided to Third Parties for a fee.
   (e) Personal Use. An individual may use the Licensed Products for
   Non-Commercial Use.

   4.3. Licensed Products: Paid Use (SUBSCRIPTION REQUIRED)
   Any other use of a Licensed Product requires a Subscription. This
   includes, in particular, use by or on behalf of any Legal Entity that
   is not a Micro-Company, an Educational Institution, or a Non-Profit
   Organization, other than Evaluation. The fee for a Subscription is
   set by the Band that contains the number of Employees of the
   Organization, according to the Licensor's price list in effect at
   the time of purchase or renewal (published at
   https://dataisland.ai/pricing), or as stated in the Order.

   4.4. Companies Under Ten Employees That Are Not Micro-Companies
   An Organization with fewer than ten (10) Employees that is not a
   Micro-Company (for example, because its annual turnover and its
   annual balance sheet total both exceed EUR 2,000,000) needs a
   Subscription, and its Band is the lowest Band of the price list
   (currently named "Small").

   4.5. Scope of a Subscription
   A Subscription covers the whole Organization, including every
   Affiliate, with unlimited Authorized Users, data, Instances, and
   Environments, as described in Section 3.2. One Order may cover both
   Licensed Products.

   4.6. Declaration and Confirmation
   The Organization declares its number of Employees when it purchases
   a Subscription, and confirms it at each renewal, in good faith and
   based on its most recent annual report and its current number of
   Long-Term Contractors.

   4.7. Growth
   If the number of Employees grows beyond the Band during a term, the
   Band and the fee do not change for the rest of that term. At
   renewal, the Band that contains the confirmed number of Employees
   applies, whether it is higher or lower, so an Organization that has
   grown moves up to the next Band at renewal. Legal Entities that the
   Organization acquires or establishes during a term are covered for
   the rest of that term. If the Licensee itself becomes an Affiliate of
   a larger group, the Subscription continues to cover only the
   Organization as it was before that change, until renewal.

   4.8. Term and Renewal
   A Subscription runs for the term stated in the Order (normally
   twelve (12) months) and renews as the Order provides. If it expires
   or is not renewed, the right to use the Licensed Products under it
   ends, unless the Organization qualifies under Section 4.2. Expiry
   does not affect Your Content or Your use of the Free Products.

   4.9. Order Terms
   Support, the Enterprise add-on, hosting, services, discounts,
   payment, and data-processing terms are set by the Order and by the
   Licensor's terms referred to in it. If an Order conflicts with this
   License, the Order prevails for that Subscription.

5. Restrictions

   5.1. What You May Not Do
   Except as this License expressly allows, or as a Partner Agreement
   expressly authorizes, You may not, and may not allow or help anyone
   else to:
   (a) modify the Software, or create, use, or distribute a
   Modification or a Derivative Work, except as Sections 3.1(e), 6.4,
   and 15.1 allow;
   (b) reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble any part of the
   Software, except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits
   it despite this restriction (Section 15.1);
   (c) remove, alter, or obscure this License or any license,
   copyright, trademark, or other notice in or with the Software; every
   copy that You make must include this License;
   (d) circumvent, disable, remove, or tamper with any License Key or
   license-verification mechanism, or create, share, or use any License
   Key other than one that the Licensor issued for Your Organization;
   (e) distribute, publish, or otherwise make copies of the Software
   available to anyone outside Your Organization (Section 5.2 sets out
   what is not distribution);
   (f) sell, resell, sublicense, rent, lease, lend, or otherwise
   transfer the Software or any right under this License, or charge a
   Third Party a fee for the Software itself;
   (g) offer the Software, or its functionality, to Third Parties as a
   Hosted Service (Section 5.3 sets out what is not a Hosted Service);
   (h) include, embed, or bundle the Software, or any part of it, in a
   product that is distributed, sold, licensed, or otherwise provided to
   Third Parties, such as software or an appliance that they install;
   (i) offer, sell, or provide a Competing Product that includes, runs,
   or is based on the Software or any part of it, or develop a Competing
   Product by copying, translating, or adapting any part of the source
   code or documentation of the Software; or
   (j) use a Licensed Product beyond the grant that applies to You, such
   as Production Use during an Evaluation.

   5.2. What Is Not Distribution
   The following are not distribution under Section 5.1(e):
   (a) making the Software available to Your Authorized Users, and to
   Service Providers acting under Section 5.5, within the grant that
   applies to Your Organization;
   (b) referring others to the Licensor's official distribution
   channels (such as its package and image registries and
   https://dataisland.ai), or declaring the Software as a dependency of
   Your own programs without including a copy of it; each recipient
   then obtains the Software from the Licensor under this License; and
   (c) giving a Third Party Your Content, as long as it contains no part
   of the Software other than code examples copied from the
   documentation under Section 3.3.

   5.3. What Is Not a Hosted Service
   Making the outputs of Your own use of the Software available to
   Third Parties is not a Hosted Service: for example, reports,
   dashboards, datasets, files, and query results built on Your data,
   including when Third Parties read data that You choose to share with
   them through the Software's data interfaces (such as REST, OData, or
   SQL endpoints). Using the Software inside Your own product or service
   whose functionality is different from that of the Software, so that
   Third Parties use Your product or service rather than the Software,
   is not a Hosted Service either, provided that it is not a Competing
   Product. Giving Third Parties access to the Software itself, its user
   interfaces, or its functionality so that they can process their own
   data, build their own content, or run their own workloads is a Hosted
   Service.

   5.4. Partner Agreements
   Reselling, distributing, offering a Hosted Service, managed operation
   on the provider's own infrastructure, embedding, OEM use, and any
   Modification beyond what this License allows are available only
   under a Partner Agreement. Contact the Licensor (Section 17).

   5.5. Consultancies and Service Providers
   A Service Provider may install, configure, operate, and support the
   Software for a client only under the client's own license under this
   License (a grant for which the client qualifies, or the client's
   Subscription), or under a Partner Agreement. Without a Partner
   Agreement:
   (a) the Software must run on infrastructure that the client
   controls, such as the client's own servers or cloud accounts;
   (b) the Service Provider may not use one client's license for
   another client or for its own purposes; and
   (c) the Service Provider's own internal use, demonstrations, and
   training need a grant of its own.
   Services that a Service Provider performs for a client under this
   Section 5.5 are not a Competing Product. The client remains
   responsible for its Service Providers' compliance with this License.

