   6.2. Building from Source
   You may build the Software from the unmodified source code that the
   Licensor provides, for use under Section 3. The result is subject to
   this License like any other copy of the Software.

   6.3. Errors and Fixes
   If You find an error in the Software, You may report it to the
   Licensor. The Licensor decides whether and how to correct it,
   normally through an update. Installing the updates, patches, and new
   versions that the Licensor provides is not a Modification.

   6.4. Proposed Changes
   You may change a copy of the source code solely to prepare and test
   a Contribution, in a non-production Environment, and submit it to the
   Licensor through the channel that the Licensor designates (such as a
   pull request to its repository). You may not use or distribute the
   changed copy for any other purpose. Submitting a Contribution gives
   You no right to use the change until the Licensor releases it as part
   of the Software.

   6.5. Source-Available, Not Open Source
   The Software is source-available, not open source. Access to its
   source code is provided for transparency, evaluation, security
   review, and Contributions, and does not grant any rights beyond those
   that this License expressly states.

